And then the, as far as the passage

00:18:16.745 --> 00:18:20.345
of water through the, through the, crossing,

00:18:21.385 --> 00:18:22.665
there will be two,

00:18:24.265 --> 00:18:24.905
culverts,

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:27.140
two styles of culverts installed

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:30.980
on the western side closer to Pine Ridge.

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:36.420
That is going to be a three foot by eight foot concrete

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:37.700
box culvert

00:18:38.025 --> 00:18:40.425
that will be embedded into the ground,

00:18:40.665 --> 00:18:41.545
25%.

00:18:41.545 --> 00:18:43.625
I think it will be buried about nine inches.

00:18:45.945 --> 00:18:47.785
On the other side would be a,

00:18:48.345 --> 00:18:53.385
round culvert pipe, probably what most people are accustomed to seeing. It would be three foot in diameter.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:56.850
On

00:18:57.170 --> 00:19:00.290
both sides we would have what's called riprap,

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:02.050
installed to,

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:07.490
manage the rate of the flow of water, re disperse it into a more natural,

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:09.170
pattern of flow

00:19:09.735 --> 00:19:11.095
with the way that the water

00:19:11.575 --> 00:19:12.775
flows today

00:19:13.815 --> 00:19:14.455
and,

00:19:14.695 --> 00:19:16.935
this system has been engineered,

00:19:17.415 --> 00:19:18.135
to

00:19:19.575 --> 00:19:22.135
pass the one hundred year storm,

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.460
meaning there's a 1%

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:26.740
or less,

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:29.620
1% or less chance of the event happening,

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:31.940
in any given year.

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:34.420
It's designed to pass it with

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:35.860
very, very little,

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:39.885
effects to the surface elevation of the water,

00:19:41.085 --> 00:19:44.685
as compared to the crossing not being there at all. In fact,

00:19:45.645 --> 00:19:46.765
if you go

00:19:47.325 --> 00:19:49.965
not a very long way up 50 to 100 feet,

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:54.120
this, a really rare rainstorm event

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:55.080
would,

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:58.120
you would only see water levels increase about

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:01.240
nine inches, I believe is what the engineer's report said,

